; Client environment reference.
;
; Every variable the client reads is listed here. They are read at build time (or when the dev
; server starts) from the shell, then `packages/client/.env`, then the root `.env`, and inlined
; into the bundle by `build-env.ts` -- so they end up in public JavaScript: never put a secret here.
; Variables marked [shared] are also read by the server, so they belong in the root `.env` (see
; the root `.env.template`). They are commented out here on purpose: a value in
; `packages/client/.env` overrides the root one for the client only, so uncomment one only to give
; the client a different value from the server.
;
; Use the names below, not `VITE_*` ones. Vite also loads `VITE_`-prefixed variables from this
; package's `.env` files on its own, but `build-env.ts` overrides every `VITE_*` name the app reads,
; so setting one directly has no effect.
;
; Conventions: active entries are required; commented-out `# VAR=value` entries are optional, or
; [shared] and set in the root `.env`.
; `src/__tests__/env-template.test.ts` keeps this file in sync with `build-env.ts`.
;
; Deployed builds get these from the CI job environment (.github/workflows/client-publish.yml), not
; from a file.

########
# Auth #
########

; Auth0. Required unless ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=1 (without them sign-in cannot start).
; Client ID of the Auth0 Single Page Application the client signs in with
; (docs/user-authentication-plan/auth0-setup.md §2.1).
AUTH0_FRONTEND_CLIENT_ID=your_spa_client_id
; Tenant domain as a bare hostname, and the API audience the access token is requested for
; [shared]: set them in the root `.env` (the server verifies tokens with the same values);
; uncomment here only to override them for the client.
# AUTH0_DOMAIN=your-tenant.us.auth0.com
# AUTH0_AUDIENCE=https://api.accounter.com

; Local development only [shared]: `1` skips Auth0 and sends an `X-Dev-Auth` header as
; DEV_AUTH_USER_ID instead. The server only honours it with ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=1 on its side, and it
; never reads this file: set it in the root .env (or packages/server/.env) for that. Default: off.
# ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=1
; With ALLOW_DEV_AUTH=1: the business_users.user_id to act as (`yarn seed:staging-demo` prints an
; admin and an accountant id). Without it, no dev-auth header is sent.
# DEV_AUTH_USER_ID=

###########
# Backend #
###########

; GraphQL endpoint. Unset uses the default for the Vite mode: http://localhost:4000/graphql in dev,
; the hosted staging or production URL for `--mode staging` / production builds. Set it for preview
; deploys, branch environments, or to point a local client at another backend.
# GRAPHQL_URL=http://localhost:4000/graphql
